{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 10,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[ MUSIC ]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4890,
    "dDurationMs": 4930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Power of Light - presented by Science@NASA"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9820,
    "dDurationMs": 8790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Crewmembers on the International Space Station (ISS) can experience sunrises and sunsets in rapid succession -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18610,
    "dDurationMs": 5010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about 16 \"sunsets\" per day because the space station circles Earth once every 90 minutes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23620,
    "dDurationMs": 5710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most people function regularly on a 24-hour cycle known as a circadian rhythm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29330,
    "dDurationMs": 7100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However the space station environment creates a departure from the cycle of light and dark astronauts are used to at home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36430,
    "dDurationMs": 7260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A high workload, the need to work 'nightshifts', the excitement of spaceflight, plus the unusual environment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43690,
    "dDurationMs": 8050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can disrupt astronauts' circadian clocks. These factors can combine to disrupt sleep, which can in turn effect performance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51740,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Being wide awake when they should be sleeping is in fact a long-standing challenge among ISS crewmembers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58380,
    "dDurationMs": 8720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Studies of astronauts who flew between 2001-2011 on the space shuttle and 2006-2011 on the station"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67100,
    "dDurationMs": 4970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "showed that astronauts slept considerably less in space than they did on Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72070,
    "dDurationMs": 6180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "About 3/4 of them reported using sleep promoting pills during their 6-month missions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78250,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Use of caffeine is also commonplace among ISS astronauts to fight off the daytime drowsies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82900,
    "dDurationMs": 6030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But NASA is seeking a better way to solve the problem. The secret lies in light itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88930,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's known that the blue-enriched light emitted by our laptops can keep us awake at night."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93590,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A new NASA study will investigate how to use that for the benefit of humankind, and not just on the ISS."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101590,
    "dDurationMs": 7070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This light study -- known as the Lighting Effects study -- coincides with a lighting 'makeover' on the space station."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108660,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The fluorescent lights on the station are being replaced with a new system of solid-state light-emitting diodes (LEDs)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115340,
    "dDurationMs": 6890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not only are the LEDs more energy-efficient and safer, they can literally shed all sorts of light on the study topic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122230,
    "dDurationMs": 6690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brigham and Women's Hospital's Dr. Steven Lockley and Thomas Jefferson University's Dr. George Brainard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128920,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are the co-principal investigators of the Lighting Effects study."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132400,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lockley explains: \"Light has a number of effects on our sleep and circadian rhythms;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136810,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a natural stimulant and can improve alertness and performance, and also help reset the 24-hour clock when it gets out of sync."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144090,
    "dDurationMs": 7230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The human eye contains a light-sensitive protein called melanopsin, different from the rods and cones that we use to see,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151320,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which detects light in the eye and mediates these effect. Melanopsin is most sensitive to short-wavelength blue light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158920,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so by increasing or decreasing the proportion of these blue wavelengths in white light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163950,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can enhance alertness, or promote sleep, respectively.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168280,
    "dDurationMs": 6260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lockley says, \"NASA has developed a multi-LED lighting system to take advantage of these light effects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174540,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The system can provide millions of different light spectra. We're not making the ISS into a disco,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180900,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we are going to use three different light settings. We'll use a general light setting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186420,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that provides a good light to see by during normal work, a higher-intensity blue light enriched setting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191200,
    "dDurationMs": 5150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that elevates alertness and can better shift the circadian clock when needed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196350,
    "dDurationMs": 6780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a lower-intensity blue wavelength-depleted 'pre-sleep' setting to calm the brain and promote sleep."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203130,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We will be studying the impact of these lights in future missions.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207220,
    "dDurationMs": 8480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Oh you guys it is so fancy, it is really awesome! I think the technical term is, light functional checkout was successful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215700,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so congratulations to the light team.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218500,
    "dDurationMs": 7240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Results of this study are expected to help define guidelines for lighting protocols during future ISS and human space missions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225740,
    "dDurationMs": 6630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Study results should make it clear exactly when and how to use these various settings of light intensity and spectrum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232370,
    "dDurationMs": 6470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These results could also lead to Earth-based benefits such as helping manage sleep patterns for shift workers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238840,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or even developing treatments for sleep disorders or jet lag."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242930,
    "dDurationMs": 6300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For more from the International Space Station, visit www.nasa.gov/station"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249230,
    "dDurationMs": 5788,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For more news about the power of light, stay tuned to science.nasa.gov."
    } ]
  } ]
}
